    {
      "type": "done",
      "answer": "No. Grace's LPDDR expansion does **not** increase the GPU's HBM capacity.\n\n**Reasoning from the lecture:**\n- The Hopper GPU \"retains local HBM,\" while Grace connects LPDDR5X through the coherent NVLink-C2C CPU–GPU link. The lecture states explicitly that \"LPDDR extends the capacity the accelerator can address; it does not enlarge HBM itself.\" See page 68 [S1].\n- The design intent is a tiered memory hierarchy: hot, latency-critical, frequently reused data stays in HBM, while large, cold objects are placed in the LPDDR capacity tier. See page 69 [S2].\n\nSo the LPDDR attached via Grace adds an additional addressable memory tier (a capacity extension), but the physical HBM on the GPU remains unchanged in size.\n\n**Sources:**\n- Page 68 [S1]\n- Page 69 [S2]",
      "citations": [
        {
          "document_id": "ad66f2c8360da43ea0981bffa549956185949044062a0abe4689381ced423402",
          "chunk_id": "ad66f2c8360da43ea0981bffa549956185949044062a0abe4689381ced423402-p68-1",
          "page": 68,
          "text": "SOTA Memory Technologies\n\nMemory Extension: LPDDR\n\n\n\n\n\n▪ Hopper retains local HBM. Grace connects LPDDR5X through the coherent\n  NVLink-C2C CPU–GPU link.\n▪ LPDDR extends the capacity the accelerator can address; it does not enlarge\n HBM itself.\n\nMemory Wall     CPU Memory     GPU Memory    SOTA Memory     Advanced AI Computing and Systems        68",
          "preview_url": "/api/documents/ad66f2c8360da43ea0981bffa549956185949044062a0abe4689381ced423402/pages/68/preview",
          "source": "S1"
        },
        {
          "document_id": "ad66f2c8360da43ea0981bffa549956185949044062a0abe4689381ced423402",
          "chunk_id": "ad66f2c8360da43ea0981bffa549956185949044062a0abe4689381ced423402-p69-1",
          "page": 69,
          "text": "SOTA Memory Technologies\n\nTiered Memory Management Decides What Stays in HBM\n\n\n\n\n\n▪ Keep hot, latency-critical, frequently reused data in HBM. Place large, cold objects\n  in the LPDDR capacity tier.\n▪ Promotion helps only when future reuse saves more than the transfer and\n  bookkeeping cost.\n\nMemory Wall     CPU Memory     GPU Memory    SOTA Memory     Advanced AI Computing and Systems        69",
          "preview_url": "/api/documents/ad66f2c8360da43ea0981bffa549956185949044062a0abe4689381ced423402/pages/69/preview",
          "source": "S2"
        }
      ],
